---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import ContactCta from "../components/ContactCta.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="About DJ Rachel Lynch | DJ Rachel Entertainment" description="Get to know DJ Rachel Lynch, event DJ and host for weddings, corporate events, and private celebrations.">
	<main id="main">
		<section class="page-hero page-width about-hero">
			<div class="page-hero__copy">
				<p class="eyebrow">My Story</p>
				<h1>The Day I Said <span class="story-heading-ending"><em>Yes</em><span class="story-heading-period">.</span></span></h1>
				<p class="hero-lead">
					I never planned to be a DJ. Crazy, right?
				</p>
				<a class="button" href="/#contact">Let’s connect</a>
			</div>
			<div class="photo-placeholder photo-placeholder--portrait">
				<span>Rachel's photo goes here</span>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="about-story">
			<div class="page-width about-story__inner">
				<p>Nearly 20 years ago, a family medical emergency left a wedding without a DJ on the day it was supposed to happen. A couple was counting on their celebration. Nobody was available to help. So I did.</p>
				<p>I was a teenager with no wedding experience, and I had no idea how I'd pull it off. But in my heart, I knew that couple deserved their wedding day. So I said yes.</p>
				<p>Somewhere in the uncertainty and stress, I found a talent I never knew I had.</p>
				<p>What started as a favor for my family and an act of love became a defining moment.</p>
				<p>So I kept saying yes. Yes to more weddings. Yes to corporate events, bigger stages, and opportunities I never could have dreamed up.</p>
				<p>Along the way, I've opened for legends like Gloria Gaynor and George Clinton &amp; Parliament-Funkadelic. I created The DJ Help Desk, a 17,000+ member community of DJs built on kindness and education. I've guest lectured at MIT and keynoted DJX Atlantic City. In 2024, I became the youngest person ever inducted into the Mobile Entertainment Expo Hall of Fame. And most importantly I've helped hundreds of couples celebrate the best days of their lives.</p>
				<p>There was no master plan. Just real passion, a willingness to learn, and one opportunity leading to the next on this crazy DJ journey of mine.</p>
				<p>Today, I still run on instinct, skill, and fearless energy, powered by a real love for music and people. Because every yes opens a world of possibilities.</p>
				<p>And I'm so glad I said yes.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<ContactCta />
	</main>
</SiteLayout>
